===Meet up with the Landau siblings at the Overworld cable car{{subst:void|<!--201140302-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Administrative District|update|It is about time to meet the Landau siblings. According to Gepard, you are absolutely required for this Underworld trip with the Guards &mdash; and you like hearing this.<br />As it is, why don't you go to the Overworld cable car and meet up with the Landau siblings.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Gepard)
----
:'''Gepard:''' (Trailblazer), you're here. Thanks again for agreeing to this.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sorry to keep you waiting.
::'''Gepard:''' Don't be, I only just arrived myself.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You look like you only just got here...
::'''Gepard:''' You're not wrong, it's only been a few minutes.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What about the rest of the Garrison?
::'''Gepard:''' They're behind us. If negotiations go well, then Dunn will lead them down into the Underworld.
::'''Gepard:''' He's a very capable sergeant &mdash; upright, plainspoken &mdash; a model Silvermane Guard.
::'''Gepard:''' ...I assume you remember him? You and Serval ambushed &mdash; uh... subdued him in the Silvermane Guard Restricted Zone. I think he was out cold for most of the action.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It was an accident...
:::'''Gepard:''' The conflict was a product of the situation, I understand.
:::'''Gepard:''' Not to mention... he wasn't in bad shape when we found him. Thank you for holding back.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sometimes fights lead to friendship!
:::'''Gepard:''' The conflict was a product of the situation, I understand.
:::'''Gepard:''' Not to mention... he wasn't in bad shape when we found him. Thank you for holding back.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What was that "bygones" thing you said again...?
:::'''Gepard:''' He wasn't in bad shape when we found him. Thank you for holding back.
::'''Gepard:''' Don't worry, the hard work is already behind us.
:'''Gepard:''' The highest priority for today is establishing good negotiations with the chief of Wildfire &mdash; I'm about to get that process underway. Serval was a little delayed on the way over, but that doesn't affect our schedule. Let's set off.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Alrighty.
::'''Serval:''' Hold up, I wasn't that late...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Huh, classic Serval.
::'''Serval:''' Huh? Hold up, I wasn't that late...
::'''Gepard:''' You weren't that early, either... Still, I don't blame you &mdash; you hadn't seen Mom and Dad in a long time... I'm glad you managed to speak to them.
::'''Serval:''' We didn't speak all that much... You know how it is, I can only talk to Dad for so long before I start losing it.
::'''Gepard:''' I know how it is alright. Put that to one side for now... We need to get going.
:'''Gepard:''' Negotiations will be held in the Boulder Town clinic. Serval and I are newcomers, so you'll have to lead the way, (Trailblazer).
:<!--2-second delay-->
{{Dialogue End}}

===Head to the Boulder Town clinic{{subst:void|<!--201140304-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Boulder Town|update|This is the first time that the Guards have returned to the Underworld, and the Underworld had changed greatly in the years of blockade. Criticisms for the Guards and the Supreme Guardian also swelled up throughout society there. However, the brother-sister duo of the Landau siblings and you are here to solve this problem.<br />You head to the meeting place, which is Natasha's clinic, with the Landau siblings and the Guards. The Guards from the Overworld and Wildfire from the Underworld will have a formal meeting for the first time there.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Oleg)
----
:'''Oleg:''' Well, well, well! I don't think our little clinic has ever played host to an occasion like this!
:'''Gepard:''' We meet again, Mr. Oleg.
:'''Oleg:''' Hahaha, Oleg will do, son. Oh, (Trailblazer), you probably won't know... Our young Silvermane friend here and I had the pleasure of speaking to each other at a certain guardian's succession ceremony &mdash; we're not complete strangers. But as for this young lady...
:'''Serval:''' The name's Serval. I'm, uh... an ex-engineer from the Technology Division and... Gepard's sister. Pleasure to meet you, chief!
:'''Oleg:''' Likewise, miss! The more the merrier!
:'''Oleg:''' And it's good to have you here again, (Trailblazer) &mdash; it bothered me and Natasha that we never arranged a formal welcome for you. Once we're done talking, you must all join us for a meal.
:'''Gepard:''' We'd be honored. But to your point, Oleg &mdash; let's finish our discussions first.
:'''Oleg:''' Quite right. Let's head inside &mdash; too much commotion out here.
----
:'''Gepard:''' The Underworld... isn't exactly how I remember it.
:'''Serval:''' ...Feels like we're not getting many friendly looks, huh.
{{Dialogue End}}

===Listen to the meeting between the Silvermane Guards and Wildfire{{subst:void|<!--201140305-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Natasha's Clinic|update|The two parties of the meetings have arrived. Though there are very few places to sit in the clinic, you might as well find a spot to audit this "official" meeting.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Natasha)
----
:'''Natasha:''' ...So she's your sister. The Landau family is full of talented young people I see.
:'''Oleg:''' You're worried that Underworlders might still hold a grudge against the Silvermane Guards, so you want to show your solidarity with the Trailblazers to build some trust. Seems like a sound strategy to me.
:'''Gepard:''' Rebuilding trust between the two worlds has always been a priority for Lady Bronya.
:'''Gepard:''' People here must have felt abandoned by the Guards after the passage was sealed off. If we were to simply "take over" the Underworld in the name of the supreme guardian... I can only imagine how people would react.
:'''Oleg:''' Seems like you have a good handle on the situation. I see now why you made captain at such a young age, haha!
:'''Natasha:''' So... you're also saying the Guards want to work with Wildfire and use our reputation to win back people's support, correct?
:'''Gepard:''' ...I wouldn't use those exact words, but that is more or less what we want to achieve.
:'''Natasha:''' If that's the case, I've got a question for you:
:'''Natasha:''' Since this offer comes from those who left us to our fate for more than a decade... how would you react if Wildfire refused? Hmm? Would you use force?
:'''Serval:''' Uh... she's not trying to be diplomatic about it, is she?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Natasha won't back down easily...
::'''Serval:''' Who is she anyway...?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Starting to worry about your brother?
::'''Serval:''' Hmm... Choose your words wisely, Geppie...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Fight! Fight!
::'''Serval:''' ...Stop stoking the fire!
:'''Gepard:''' ...
:'''Gepard:''' The barrier between the surface and the underground was the product of the former supreme guardian's misjudgment and the policies that resulted from it. The people of Belobog should have stood together, but instead we were made to blame and hate one another...
:'''Gepard:''' Lady Bronya wants Belobog to heal, so the Silvermane Guards need to regain the people's trust. But we won't achieve that by kicking doors open and policing everyone around.
:'''Gepard:''' As a grassroots organization, Wildfire did an extraordinary job maintaining order for over a decade in the absence of the Guards. I can only imagine how much work you put in to protect the Underworld.
:'''Gepard:''' I can assure you that the Guards are not here to seize power. If it takes time for the people to trust us, so be it. We're willing to take small measures and serve as an auxiliary force to Wildfire to help maintain peace.
:'''Gepard:''' I hope you can see that everything we do, we do to rebuild trust and make Belobog work for all.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} He thought of everything! That's a true captain for you.
::'''Serval:''' I swear he never used to be this emotionally intelligent...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Lil' Geppie has grown up...
::'''Serval:''' I've never really seen this side of him before... the more you learn.
:'''Natasha:''' ...That's an answer I can accept. Oleg, what do you think?
:'''Oleg:''' Haha, I think there's no need for the guessing game to continue. It's obvious we share the same goal.
:'''Oleg:''' With the help of Bronya, Serval, and Gepard, we're one step closer to rebuilding a united Belobog.
:'''Natasha:''' I agree. Tell Bronya that Wildfire will work with the Silvermane Guards on security matters. However, things aren't simple down here &mdash; please also tell her to draw up plans in case the situation demands&mdash;
:'''Voice outside the Clinic:''' M&mdash;Monsters! Monsters from the Fragmentum!
:'''Voice outside the Clinic:''' They're swarming toward the town!
:'''Oleg:''' Not good... Stay here, Natasha &mdash; the patients need you. The soldiers and I will handle this.
:'''Natasha:''' ...Understood. We'll be counting on you.
----
:'''(Trailblazer):''' (Everyone rushed outside... I should probably see what's happening.)
{{Dialogue End}}

===Leave the clinic and see what is happening{{subst:void|<!--201140307-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Boulder Town|update|The meeting was progressing smoothly until the sudden noises from outside disturbed the harmonious mood in the room. Your friends instantly rush out the door to see what is going on. "They are indeed leaders of both sides of Belobog," you think, "and I'm just here to fill the seats."<br />Complaints aside, you instinctively feel that the problems that follow might be your specialty &mdash; fighting, and saving the world on the side &mdash; anyways, head outside and check out the situation.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Miner)
----
:'''Terrified Refugee:''' P&mdash;Please, help my friends!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What happened?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why don't you finish your story first?
::'''Terrified Refugee:''' I&mdash;I'm sorry! I didn't mean to scare you all...
::'''Gepard:''' What happened? Take a breather.
:'''Terrified Refugee:''' Th&mdash;The monsters invaded the mine! Please, you have to save my friends!
:'''Terrified Refugee:''' Otherwise, those things will t&mdash;tear them apart!
:'''Gepard:''' Don't worry, the Silvermane Guards are trained for these situations. Where do we find them?
:'''Terrified Refugee:''' The Great Mine! The one with the b&mdash;big ore vein...!
:'''Gepard:''' Understood. I'll send my men to set up a perimeter and start the rescue operation right away.
:'''Gepard:''' Mr. Oleg, please entrust the Silvermane Guards with the rescue.
:'''Gepard:''' The defense of Boulder Town will need Wildfire's expertise. Watch out for ambushes and be ready to receive wounded soldiers.
:'''Oleg:''' Ha, you're a natural-born commander. Understood, leave it to me, son.
:'''Oleg:''' Your troops will be unfamiliar with the layout of the mine &mdash; I'll send some of my men to be your guides.
:'''Gepard:''' ...Thank you. In the name of the Preservation, I promise we'll do everything we can to save lives.
:'''Gepard:''' I'll go on ahead and lead the troops to the mine. (Trailblazer), Serval, catch up to us when you can.
----
{{Dialogue End}}

===Talk with Serval and head to the Great Mine{{subst:void|<!--201140308-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Boulder Town|update|Hearing news that the Great Mine is invaded by Fragmentum monsters, the Guards and Wildfire instantly form a coalition and Gepard is already leading the vanguards to the incident site.<br />It is the duty of Trailblazers to save people &mdash; once you are ready, head out with Serval.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Serval)
:'''Serval:''' You know the way to the Great Mine, right? Let's catch up with Gepard when you're ready!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm ready.
::'''Serval:''' That's all you needed to say! Let's go.
